{
  "_comment": [
    "Benchmark corpora. Each entry names an archive to download and the payload inside it",
    "that is fed to the compressors.",
    "",
    "kind=tree: the payload is a directory in the archive. The driver re-tars it WITHOUT",
    "compression into one input file, with sorted names and zeroed timestamps so the input",
    "is byte-identical on every run and machine. This is the unit measured.",
    "",
    "kind=files: the payload is a set of loose files. Each file is its own corpus id",
    "(\"<id>/<name>\"), which is how the Silesia corpus is normally reported.",
    "",
    "Versions are pinned so a cached baseline stays comparable; bump the version and the",
    "cache key changes with it. Every URL is the project's own release host:",
    "  Linux      cdn.kernel.org/pub/linux/kernel/v7.x/  (7.0 released 2026-04-12)",
    "  LLVM/Clang github.com/llvm/llvm-project/releases  (llvmorg-23.1.2, 2026-09-22)",
    "  CPython    python.org/ftp/python/                 (3.14.8, 2026-09-30)",
    "  Redis      download.redis.io/releases/            (8.10.2, 2026-07-29)",
    "  Silesia    mattmahoney.net/dc/silesia.html        (the surviving mirror; the",
    "             original sun.aei.polsl.pl host is gone)"
  ],
